Fast Flow and Minizip folders are required.

# Compile

To compile simply execute the comand Make in the directory where the file `MakeFile` is contained.

Execute the `mapping_string.sh` script in the Fast Flow directory.

# Execute

To execute the sequential version only 2 input are required:

`./SEQ_minizip [c or d] [Path to Folder or file]`

 where `c`is for compressing and `d` for decompressing.

To execute the sequential version 4 input are required:

`./FF_minizip [c or d] [Path to Folder or file] [Number of Left Workers] [Number of Right Workers]`

where `c`is for compressing and `d` for decompressing. The last two numbers are needed to specify for the numberof workers in the All2All implemented in Fast Flow.

To execute the sequential version 4 input are required:

`mpirun -np [Number Of Nodes] ./MPI_minizip [c or d] [Path to Folder or file] [Number of Right Workers]` 

where the first number is the number of nodes, `c`is for compressing and `d` for decompressing. The last number is the number of Right Workers in the All2All.


# Run the test

To run the test go to the directory scripts using the comand `cd scripts`.

Make sure all the scripts have the right permissions, to do that for all the files in the folder use the command `chmod -R +x ./`.

Using `sbatch ./[NameOfTheScript]`is possible to execute the script in the cluster.

In local just `./[NameOfTheScript]`.
